# Claude Tetris

Vanilla browser Tetris. No package.json, bundler, framework, or tests.

## Tech Stack
- HTML5 + CSS3 + JavaScript ES6+ (`'use strict'`)
- Canvas 2D API (`#board`, `#next-canvas`)
- `requestAnimationFrame` game loop
- Zero npm/runtime deps

## Commands
```bash
# Dev (recommended)
python3 -m http.server 8000
# or: npx serve .
# or: open index.html / xdg-open index.html
```
No build, test, or lint scripts.

## Project Layout
```
/
  index.html   # DOM: board canvas 300x600, HUD, overlay, loads game.js
  style.css    # Dark arcade UI; flex layout; overlay blur
  game.js      # All game logic (~300 lines, single file)
  README.md
```

## Code Standards
- Keep logic in `game.js`; markup IDs must stay in sync with `getElementById` usage.
- Board model: `ROWS x COLS` matrix; cell `0` empty, `1-7` piece color index (`COLORS`/`PIECES`).
- Tunables at top of `game.js`: `COLS`, `ROWS`, `BLOCK`, `COLORS`, `PIECES`, `LINE_SCORES`, `dropInterval`.
- If changing `COLS`/`ROWS`/`BLOCK`, update `#board` canvas `width`/`height` (`COLS*BLOCK` x `ROWS*BLOCK`).
- Prefer plain functions; no modules/imports; browser globals OK for this size.

## Constraints
- NEVER add frameworks, bundlers, TypeScript, or npm deps unless explicitly requested.
- NEVER split into a build pipeline; ship static files only.
- Preserve classic Tetris rules: 7 pieces, wall kicks via `tryRotate`, scoring `[0,100,300,500,800]*level`, level every 10 lines, ghost piece.
- Do not break keyboard map: Left/Right move, Up/X rotate, Down soft drop, Space hard drop, P pause.
- Keep English UI strings in HTML/overlay unless asked to change locale.
- Hold: C/Shift; modes: Classic, Challenge (40 lines / 2 min), Arcade (power-ups + special pieces).
- Power-ups and non-standard pieces only in Arcade mode.
